WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.852 --> 00:00:04.577
- [Narrator] This is
Picasso, a Senegalese parrot.

00:00:04.577 --> 00:00:06.373
(gentle instrumental music)

00:00:06.373 --> 00:00:07.902
Due to their popularity,

00:00:07.902 --> 00:00:12.069
they are one of the most heavily
trapped birds in the world.

00:00:13.161 --> 00:00:14.963
Spread throughout Western Africa,

00:00:14.963 --> 00:00:17.690
they live in open woodlands and savannas

00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:21.857
and feed on fruit, seeds, buds
and occasionally crop items.

00:00:23.557 --> 00:00:27.086
Senegalese parrots are
only about nine inches long

00:00:27.086 --> 00:00:29.336
and weigh up to six ounces.

00:00:30.998 --> 00:00:32.809
They may be small in size,

00:00:32.809 --> 00:00:34.736
but they're a gregarious bunch

00:00:34.736 --> 00:00:38.223
with lively, energetic personalities.

00:00:38.223 --> 00:00:40.259
Their dark gray faces are complemented

00:00:40.259 --> 00:00:43.573
by green and yellow
plumage across their body.

00:00:43.573 --> 00:00:47.336
Senegalese parrots are
incredibly popular pets,

00:00:47.336 --> 00:00:49.886
which has made the
trade, import and export

00:00:49.886 --> 00:00:52.469
of wild-caught parrots illegal.

00:00:54.586 --> 00:00:58.336
This is the Senegalese parrot.

